# Fixtures, not projects: everything here is generated by running them.
#
# The three directories below are built by `zig build test-diagnostics`, which
# runs a real `spago build` in each. `spago` writes `spago.lock` on the first
# run; purzig writes `.purzig/` (the package set, the backend shim, the
# `spago` wrapper and the captured output of the last failing command) before
# spago starts. None of it is source.
#
# `.purzig/`, `output/`, `output-zig/` and `.spago/` are already ignored by the
# repository's root `.gitignore`; `spago.lock` is NOT, and a lock file generated
# by a fixture has no business being committed.
*/spago.lock
